c\u00b2)/2, but in reality, the radius of the sphere enclosing the box is equal to half the space diagonal, so r = (1/2)\u221a(a\u00b2 +b\u00b2 +c\u00b2). So, r\u00b2= (a\u00b2 +b\u00b2 +c\u00b2)/4.\n\nWait, that's correct. So, the sphere radius squared is (a\u00b2 +b\u00b2 +c\u00b2)/4.\n\nSo, in Case 1, where a=23/4, b=23/4, c=23/(2\u221a6). Wait, hold on, no.\n\nWait, no, earlier in Case 1, we had a=23/4, b=23/4, c=23/(2\u221a6). Wait, that might not be correct.\n\nWait, let me backtrack.\n\nWe had the constraints:\n\n2(ab + bc + ca) =54, so ab + bc + ca=27.\n\nAnd abc=23.\n\nSo, in Case 1, when b=c=2, then a=23/(2*2)=23/4.\n\nSo, a=23/4, b=2, c=2.\n\nThus, a\u00b2 +b\u00b2 +c\u00b2=(529/16) +4 +4=529/16 +8=529/16 +128/16=657/16.\n\nThus, r\u00b2=(657/16)/4=657/64.\n\nSimilarly, in Case 2, when b= -1 +2\u221a6, which is approximately 3.898.\n\nThen, a=23/(b*c). Since b=c= -1 +2\u221a6.\n\nWait, b=c= -1 +2\u221a6, so a=23/(b^2).\n\nCompute a=23/(b\u00b2)=23/( ( -1 +2\u221a6 )\u00b2 )=23/(1 -4\u221a6 +24)=23/(25 -4\u221a6 ).\n\nSo, a=23/(25 -4\u221a6 ).\n\nThen, a\u00b2 +b\u00b2 +c\u00b2= a\u00b2 +2b\u00b2= [23\u00b2/(25 -4\u221a6 )\u00b2 ] +2*(25 -4\u221a6 ).\n\nCompute numerator:\n\n=529/(625 -200\u221a6 + 96) +50 -8\u221a6\n\nWait, no:\n\nWait, a\u00b2=529/(625 -200\u221a6 + 96). Wait, denominator is (25 -4\u221a6 )\u00b2=625 - 2*25*4\u221a6 + (4\u221a6 )\u00b2=625 -200\u221a6 +96=721 -200\u221a6.\n\nThus, a\u00b2=529/(721 -200\u221a6 ).\n\nThen, a\u00b2 +2b\u00b2=529/(721 -200\u221a6 ) +2*(25 -4\u221a6 ).\n\nSo, r\u00b2=(a\u00b2 +2b\u00b2)/4=(529/(721 -200\u221a6 ) +50 -8\u221a6 )/4.\n\nThis is getting complicated. Maybe there's a better way.\n\nWait, perhaps we can express 529/(721 -200\u221a6 ). Multiply numerator and denominator by (721 +200\u221a6 ):\n\n=529*(721 +200\u221a6 )/(721\u00b2 - (200\u221a6 )\u00b2 )\n\nCompute denominator: 721\u00b2 - (200\u221a6 )\u00b2= 721\u00b2 -200\u00b2*6=519841 -240000=279841.\n\nSo, a\u00b2=529*(721 +200\u221a6 )/279841.\n\nThus, a\u00b2 +2b\u00b2=529*(721 +200\u221a6 )/279841 +50 -8\u221a6.\n\nThis is still messy. Maybe we need a different approach.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps the minimal r\u00b2 occurs at Case 1 where a=23/4, b=2, c=2.\n\nBut let me check if that's actually minimal.\n\nWait, if I can show that a\u00b2 +b\u00b2 +c\u00b2 is minimized when a=23/4, b=2, c=2, then that would be our answer.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps we can use the method of Lagrange multipliers for two constraints.\n\nWait, the problem has two constraints: ab + bc + ca=27 and abc=23.\n\nSo, we have to minimize a\u00b2 +b\u00b2 +c\u00b2.\n\nLet me try to express variables in terms of each other.\n\nLet me denote x=a, y=b, z=c.\n\nGiven:\n\nxy + yz + zx=27,\n\nxyz=23,\n\nand minimize x\u00b2 +y\u00b2 +z\u00b2.\n\nLet me try to express variables in terms of two variables.\n\nFrom xyz=23, we can express z=23/(xy).\n\nPlug into the first equation:\n\nxy + y*(23/(xy)) +x*(23/(xy))=27\n\nSimplify:\n\nxy + (23/y) + (23/x)=27.\n\nSo, we have:\n\nxy +23*(1/x +1/y)=27.\n\nLet me denote u=1/x, v=1/y.\n\nThen, equation becomes:\n\n(1/u)(1/v) +23(u +v)=27.\n\nWait, that might not be helpful.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps set x=y, to see if the minimal occurs when two variables are equal.\n\nLet me assume x=y, then z=23/(x\u00b2).\n\nThen, the first equation becomes x\u00b2 +x*z +x*z= x\u00b2 +2xz=27.\n\nBut z=23/x\u00b2, so:\n\nx\u00b2 +2x*(23/x\u00b2)=27 =>x\u00b2 +46/x=27.\n\nMultiply both sides by x:\n\nx\u00b3 +46=27x =>x\u00b3 -27x +46=0.\n\nTry to find rational roots:\n\nPossible roots: \u00b11, \u00b12, \u00b123, \u00b146.\n\nTest x=1:1 -27 +46=20\u22600.\n\nx=2:8 -54 +46=0. Bingo! So, x=2 is a root.\n\nThus, factor as (x -2)(x\u00b2 +2x -23)=0.\n\nSo, x=2, or x=(-2 \u00b1\u221a(4 +92))/2=(-2 \u00b1\u221a96)/2=-1 \u00b12\u221a6.\n\nSince x>0, x=2 or x=-1 +2\u221a6\u22483.898.\n\nThus, when x=y=2, z=23/4.\n\nWhich gives a\u00b2 +b\u00b2 +c\u00b2=4 +4 + (23/4)\u00b2=8 +529/16=128/16 +529/16=657/16.\n\nAlternatively, when x=y\u22483.898, z\u224823/(3.898)^2\u224823/15.2\u22481.513.\n\nCompute a\u00b2 +b\u00b2 +c\u00b2\u2248(3.898)^2 + (3.898)^2 + (1.513)^2\u224815.198 +15.198 +2.295\u224832.691.\n\nWhich is less than 657/16\u224840.8125.\n\nSo, this is a smaller value.\n\nBut wait, is this the minimal?\n\nWait, 32.691 is less than 40.8125, so perhaps this is the minimal.\n\nBut is this the minimal? Or can we get even smaller?\n\nWait, 32.691 is approximately 32.69, which is 657/16\u224840.8125 vs. 32.69.\n\nBut 32.69 is less, so it's a better minimal.\n\nBut we need to find an exact value.\n\nSo, in the case where x=y=-1 +2\u221a6, then a\u00b2 +b\u00b2 +c\u00b2=2x\u00b2 +z\u00b2, where z=23/x\u00b2.\n\nThus, compute 2x\u00b2 + (23/x\u00b2)^2.\n\nWait, x= -1 +2\u221a6, so x\u00b2=(1 -4\u221a6 +24)=25 -4\u221a6.\n\nThus, 2x\u00b2=50 -8\u221a6.\n\nCompute z=23/x\u00b2=23/(25 -4\u221a6 ).\n\nMultiply numerator and denominator by (25 +4\u221a6 ):\n\nz=23*(25 +4\u221a6 )/(25\u00b2 - (4\u221a6 )\u00b2)= (575 +92\u221a6 )/(625 - 96)= (575 +92\u221a6 )/529.\n\nThus, z\u00b2= (575 +92\u221a6 )\u00b2 /529\u00b2.\n\nWait, no, z is a length, so z= (575 +92\u221a6 )/529.\n\nWait, but we need z\u00b2.\n\nWait, no, z=23/(25 -4\u221a6 ). So, z\u00b2=529/(25 -4\u221a6 )\u00b2=529/(625 -200\u221a6 +96)=529/(721 -200\u221a6 ).\n\nAgain, rationalizing:\n\nMultiply numerator and denominator by (721 +200\u221a6 ):\n\nz\u00b2=529*(721 +200\u221a6 )/(721\u00b2 - (200\u221a6 )\u00b2)=529*(721 +200\u221a6 )/(519841 - 240000))=529*(721 +200\u221a6 )/279841.\n\nThus, z\u00b2= (529*721 +529*200\u221a6 )/279841.\n\nCompute 529*721: 529*700=370,300; 529*21=11,109; total=370,300 +11,109=381,409.\n\nCompute 529*200=105,800.\n\nThus, z\u00b2= (381,409 +105,800\u221a6 )/279,841.\n\nThus, a\u00b2 +b\u00b2 +c\u00b2=50 -8\u221a6 + (381,409 +105,800\u221a6 )/279,841.\n\nWait, wait, no. Wait, a\u00b2 +b\u00b2 +c\u00b2=2x\u00b2 +z\u00b2=2*(25 -4\u221a6 ) + z\u00b2=50 -8\u221a6 + z\u00b2.\n\nBut z\u00b2=(381,409 +105,800\u221a6 )/279,841.\n\nThus, a\u00b2 +b\u00b2 +c\u00b2=50 -8\u221a6 + (381,409 +105,800\u221a6 )/279,841.\n\nConvert 50 to 279,841 denominator:\n\n50=13,992,050/279,841.\n\nSimilarly, -8\u221a6= -8\u221a6*(279,841/279,841)= -2,238,728\u221a6 /279,841.\n\nThus,\n\na\u00b2 +b\u00b2 +c\u00b2= (13,992,050 -2,238,728\u221a6 +381,409 +105,800\u221a6 )/279,841.\n\nCombine like terms:\n\nNumerator= (13,992,050 +381,409 ) + (-2,238,728\u221a6 +105,800\u221a6 )=14,373,459 + (-2,132,928\u221a6 ).\n\nThus,\n\na\u00b2 +b\u00b2 +c\u00b2= (14,373,459 -2,132,928\u221a6 )/279,841.\n\nThis is getting too complicated. Maybe I need a different approach.\n\nWait, perhaps instead of trying to solve for a, b, c, think about the relationship between a, b, c.\n\nGiven that 2(ab + bc + ca)=54, so ab + bc + ca=27, and abc=23.\n\nWe need to minimize (a\u00b2 +b\u00b2 +c\u00b2)/4, which is r\u00b2.\n\nSo, r\u00b2=(a\u00b2 +b\u00b2 +c\u00b2)/4.\n\nWe need to find the minimum of a\u00b2 +b\u00b2 +c\u00b2 given that ab + bc + ca=27 and abc=23.\n\nI remember that for positive real numbers, a\u00b2 +b\u00b2 +c\u00b2 \u2265 (ab + bc + ca). So, 27 is the minimum, but we have a specific constraint with abc=23.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use the inequality that relates a\u00b2 +b\u00b2 +c\u00b2 and (ab + bc + ca). For three variables, a\u00b2 +b\u00b2 +c\u00b2 \u2265 (ab + bc + ca). So, 27 is the minimum.\n\nBut since we have abc=23, which might be a hint that the variables are not all equal.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps use Lagrange multipliers again.\n\nLet\u2019s consider f(a,b,c)=a\u00b2 +b\u00b2 +c\u00b2.\n\nSubject to g(a,b,c)=ab + bc + ca=27 and h(a,b,c)=abc=23.\n\nWait, but it's a system of two constraints. Hmm.\n\nAlternatively, maybe express one variable in terms of others using abc=23.\n\nSay, c=23/(ab).\n\nPlug into ab + bc + ca=27:\n\nab + b*(23/(ab)) + a*(23/(ab))=27.\n\nSimplify:\n\nab + 23/(a) +23/(b)=27.\n\nLet\u2019s denote x=a, y=b.\n\nSo, we have:\n\nxy +23/x +23/y=27.\n\nWe need to minimize x\u00b2 + y\u00b2 + (23/(xy))\u00b2.\n\nWait, since c=23/(xy), so c\u00b2=(529)/(x\u00b2 y\u00b2).\n\nSo, the function to minimize is x\u00b2 + y\u00b2 +529/(x\u00b2 y\u00b2).\n\nThis seems difficult, but maybe assume that x=y, due to symmetry.\n\nLet\u2019s set x=y.\n\nThen, the equation becomes:\n\nx\u00b2 +23/x +23/x=27.\n\nSimplify:\n\nx\u00b2 +46/x=27.\n\nMultiply both sides by x:\n\nx\u00b3 +46=27x.\n\nThus, x\u00b3 -27x +46=0.\n\nLet\u2019s try to find rational roots.\n\nPossible roots: factors of 46 over 1, which are \u00b11, \u00b12, \u00b123, \u00b146.\n\nTest x=1:1 -27 +46=20\u22600.\n\nx=2:8 -54 +46=0. Bingo!\n\nSo, x=2 is a root.\n\nFactor polynomial: (x -2)(x\u00b2 +2x -23)=0.\n\nThus, other roots are x=(-2 \u00b1sqrt(4 +92))/2=(-2 \u00b1sqrt(96))/2=(-2 \u00b14\u221a6)/2=-1 \u00b12\u221a6.\n\nSince x>0, x= -1 +2\u221a6\u22483.898.\n\nThus, possible x=2 or x\u22483.898.\n\nSo, when x=2, y=2, then c=23/(2*2)=23/4=5.75.\n\nThus, a=2, b=2, c=23/4.\n\nCompute a\u00b2 +b\u00b2 +c\u00b2=4 +4 + (529/16)=8 +33.0625=41.0625=657/16.\n\nThus, r\u00b2=(657/16)/4=657/64.\n\nWait, no. Wait, r\u00b2=(a\u00b2 +b\u00b2 +c\u00b2)/4=(657/16)/4=657/64.\n\nWait, but when x\u22483.898, which is -1 +2\u221a6, then a\u22483.898, b\u22483.898, c=23/(3.898)^2\u224823/15.19\u22481.514.\n\nCompute a\u00b2 +b\u00b2 +c\u00b2\u2248(15.19) + (15.19) + (2.295)=32.684\u224832.684.\n\nWhich is approximately 32.684, which is less than 41.0625.\n\nBut in exact terms, let's compute a\u00b2 +b\u00b2 +c\u00b2 when a= -1 +2\u221a6, b= -1 +2\u221a6, c=23/(a b).\n\nCompute a= -1 +2\u221a6.\n\nCompute a\u00b2= (1 -4\u221a6 +24)=25 -4\u221a6.\n\nSimilarly, b\u00b2=25 -4\u221a6.\n\nCompute ab= (-1 +2\u221a6)^2=1 -4\u221a6 +24=25 -4\u221a6.\n\nThus, c=23/(25 -4\u221a6).\n\nMultiply numerator and denominator by (25 +4\u221a6):\n\nc=23*(25 +4\u221a6)/(625 - 96)= (575 +92\u221a6)/529= (575/529) + (92\u221a6)/529.\n\nCompute c\u00b2= [575/529]^2 + 2*(575/529)*(92\u221a6)/529 + [92\u221a6/529]^2.\n\nThis seems complicated, but perhaps we can find a better way.\n\nAlternatively, note that when x= -1 +2\u221a6, then a= -1 +2\u221a6, b= -1 +2\u221a6, c=23/(ab).\n\nCompute ab= (-1 +2\u221a6)^2=1 -4\u221a6 +24=25 -4\u221a6.\n\nThus, c=23/(25 -4\u221a6)=23*(25 +4\u221a6)/(625 - 96)=23*(25 +4\u221a6)/529.\n\nWait, 529=23\u00b2, so c= (23*(25 +4\u221a6))/529= (25 +4\u221a6)/23.\n\nThus, c=25/23 + (4\u221a6)/23.\n\nThus, a= -1 +2\u221a6\u22483.898, c\u224825/23 + (4\u221a6)/23\u22481.087 +0.544\u22481.631.\n\nCompute a\u00b2 +b\u00b2 +c\u00b2=2*( (-1 +2\u221a6)^2 ) + (25/23 +4\u221a6/23)^2.\n\nCompute (-1 +2\u221a6)^2=1 -4\u221a6 +24=25 -4\u221a6.\n\nThus, 2*(25 -4\u221a6)=50 -8\u221a6.\n\nCompute c\u00b2= (25/23)^2 + 2*(25/23)*(4\u221a6/23) + (4\u221a6/23)^2=625/529 + 200\u221a6/529 + 96/529.\n\nThus, c\u00b2= (625 +96)/529 +200\u221a6/529=721/529 +200\u221a6/529.\n\nSo, a\u00b2 +b\u00b2 +c\u00b2=50 -8\u221a6 +721/529 +200\u221a6/529.\n\nConvert 50 to 50*529/529=26450/529.\n\nThus, total=26450/529 -8\u221a6 +721/529 +200\u221a6/529= (26450 +721)/529 + (-8 +200/529)\u221a6.\n\nWait, no, I think I made a miscalculation.\n\nWait, 50 is 50/1, to convert to denominator 529, it's 50*529=26450.\n\nThus, 50=26450/529.\n\nThus, a\u00b2 +b\u00b2 +c\u00b2=26450/529 +721/529 + (-8\u221a6 +200\u221a6/529).\n\nCombine terms:\n\n(26450 +721)/529 + [ (-8 +200/529) ]\u221a6.\n\nCompute 26450 +721=27171.\n\nThus, 27171/529 + [ (-8 +200/529) ]\u221a6.\n\nSimplify 27171/529: 529*51=26919, 27171-26919=252. So, 27171=529*51 +252.\n\n252/529 is as is.\n\nSo, 27171/529=51 +252/529.\n\nSimilarly, (-8 +200/529)= (-8*529 -200)/529= (-4232 -200)/529= (-4432)/529.\n\nThus, a\u00b2 +b\u00b2 +c\u00b2=51 +252/529 -4432\u221a6/529.\n\nWait, but that can't be because a\u00b2 +b\u00b2 +c\u00b2 is positive, but 4432\u221a6 is positive. Wait, no:\n\nWait, let's re-examine.\n\nWe had a\u00b2 +b\u00b2 +c\u00b2=50 -8\u221a6 + c\u00b2.\n\nBut I think I messed up in the earlier step.\n\nWait, let me try again.\n\nWait, a= -1 +2\u221a6, b= -1 +2\u221a6.\n\nCompute a\u00b2= (-1 +2\u221a6)^2=1 -4\u221a6 +24=25 -4\u221a6.\n\nSimilarly, b\u00b2=25 -4\u221a6.\n\nThus, a\u00b2 +b\u00b2=50 -8\u221a6.\n\nThen c=23/(ab)=23/(25 -4\u221a6).\n\nMultiply numerator and denominator by (25 +4\u221a6):\n\nc=23*(25 +4\u221a6)/[(25)^2 - (4\u221a6)^2]=23*(25 +4\u221a6)/(625 - 96)=23*(25 +4\u221a6)/529.\n\nThus, c= (575 +92\u221a6)/529=575/529 +92\u221a6/529.\n\nThus, c\u00b2= (575/529)^2 +2*(575/529)*(92\u221a6/529) + (92\u221a6/529)^2.\n\nWait, that's going to be messy. Maybe instead, let's compute a\u00b2 +b\u00b2 +c\u00b2.\n\nSo, a\u00b2 +b\u00b2=50 -8\u221a6.\n\nc= (575 +92\u221a6)/529.\n\nThus, c\u00b2= [575 +92\u221a6]^2 /529\u00b2.\n\nThat's a huge number, but let me compute it step by step.\n\nCompute numerator: (575 +92\u221a6)^2=575\u00b2 + 2*575*92\u221a6 + (92\u221a6)^2=330625 + 2*575*92\u221a6 + 92\u00b2*6.\n\nCompute 575*92=575*(90+2)=575*90 +575*2=51750 +1150=52900.\n\nThus, 2*575*92\u221a6=2*52900\u221a6=105800\u221a6.\n\nCompute 92\u00b2=8464, so 8464*6=50784.\n\nThus, numerator=330625 +105800\u221a6 +50784=330625 +50784=381409 +105800\u221a6.\n\nThus, c\u00b2=381409 +105800\u221a6 divided by 529\u00b2.\n\n529\u00b2=279841.\n\nThus, c\u00b2=381409/279841 +105800\u221a6 /279841.\n\nSimplify 381409/279841: divide numerator and denominator by GCD(381409,279841). Let's compute GCD(381409,279841).\n\n279841 divides into 381409 once with remainder 381409 -279841=105568.\n\nNow, GCD(279841,105568).\n\n279841 \u00f7105568=2 with remainder 279841 -2*105568=68705.\n\nGCD(105568,68705).\n\n105568 \u00f768705=1 with remainder 105568 -68705=36963.\n\nGCD(68705,36963).\n\n68705 \u00f736963=1 with remainder 68705 -36963=31742.\n\nGCD(36963,31742).\n\n36963 \u00f731742=1 with remainder 36963 -31742=5221.\n\nGCD(31742,5221).\n\n31742 \u00f75221=6 with remainder 31742 -6*5221=31742 -31726=16.\n\nGCD(5221,16).\n\n5221 \u00f716=326 with remainder 9.\n\nGCD(16,9).\n\n16 \u00f79=1 with remainder 7.\n\nGCD(9,7).\n\n9 \u00f77=1 with remainder 2.\n\nGCD(7,2).\n\n7 \u00f72=3 with remainder 1.\n\nGCD(2,1)=1.\n\nThus, GCD is 1.\n\nSo, c\u00b2=381409/279841 +105800\u221a6 /279841.\n\nThus, a\u00b2 +b\u00b2 +c\u00b2=50 -8\u221a6 +381409/279841 +105800\u221a6 /279841.\n\nCombine terms:\n\nConvert 50 to 50/1 = (50*279841)/279841=13997050/279841.\n\nSimilarly, -8\u221a6= (-8\u221a6 *279841)/279841= -2238728\u221a6 /279841.\n\nThus, a\u00b2 +b\u00b2 +c\u00b2=13997050/279841 + ( -2238728\u221a6 +105800\u221a6 ) /279841.\n\nSimplify numerator:\n\n-2238728\u221a6 +105800\u221a6= (-2238728 +105800)\u221a6= (-1182928)\u221a6.\n\nThus, a\u00b2 +b\u00b2 +c\u00b2=13997050/279841 -1182928\u221a6 /279841.\n\nFactor numerator:\n\n13997050=279841*50, because 279841*50=13997050.\n\nSimilarly, 1182928=279841* (1182928/279841). Let's compute 279841*4=1119364, which is less than 1182928. 279841*4=1119364, so 1182928-1119364=63564.\n\n63564 \u00f7279841\u22480.226, which is not integer. Wait, maybe 279841 is 529\u00b2, which is 279841. Let me check 529*529.\n\nYes, 529*529=279841.\n\nSo, 279841=529\u00b2.\n\nThus, 13997050=50*279841=50*529\u00b2.\n\nSimilarly, 1182928= (1182928/529). Let's compute 1182928 \u00f7529.\n\n529*2000=1,058,000.\n\n1,182,928 -1,058,000=124,928.\n\n529*200=105,800.\n\n124,928 -105,800=19,128.\n\n529*36=19,044.\n\n19,128 -19,044=84.\n\nSo, 529*36 +84=19,044 +84=19,128.\n\nThus, 1182928=529*2000 +529*200 +529*36 +84=529*(2000+200+36)+84=529*2236 +84.\n\nWait, this seems complicated. Maybe we can factor 529 from 1182928.\n\n1182928 \u00f7529: 529*2236=1182928? Let's check 529*2000=1,058,000; 529*236=529*(200+36)=529*200 +529*36=105,800 +19,044=124,844. So, 529*2236=529*(2000+236)=1,058,000 +124,844=1,182,844. But 1,182,844\u22601,182,928. There is a difference of 84.\n\nThus, 1182928=529*2236 +84.\n\nWait, perhaps this approach isn't helpful. Maybe just leave it as is.\n\nThus, a\u00b2 +b\u00b2 +c\u00b2= (50*279841 -1182928\u221a6)/279841= (50 - (1182928/279841)\u221a6).\n\nBut 1182928/279841= (1182928 \u00f7529)/529= (1182928 \u00f7529)=2236.164, which isn't helpful.\n\nWait, maybe factor 529 from numerator and denominator:\n\na\u00b2 +b\u00b2 +c\u00b2= [50*279841 -1182928\u221a6]/279841=50 - (1182928\u221a6)/279841.\n\nBut 1182928=2236*529 +84, so:\n\n=50 - (2236*529 +84)\u221a6 /529=50 - (2236\u221a6 +84/529).\n\nBut this seems messy. Maybe I made a miscalculation earlier.\n\nWait, maybe it's better to note that the minimal sphere enclosing the box must have radius equal to half the space diagonal of the box, which is (sqrt(a\u00b2 +b\u00b2 +c\u00b2))/2, so r\u00b2=(a\u00b2 +b\u00b2 +c\u00b2)/4.\n\nThus, if I can express a\u00b2 +b\u00b2 +c\u00b2 in terms of the given constraints, I can find r\u00b2.\n\nGiven that 2(ab + bc + ca)=54, so ab + bc + ca=27.\n\nAlso, abc=23.\n\nSo, we have variables a, b, c with ab + bc + ca=27 and abc=23.\n\nWe need to minimize a\u00b2 +b\u00b2 +c\u00b2.\n\nI recall that a\u00b2 +b\u00b2 +c\u00b2=(a +b +c)\u00b2 -2(ab + bc + ca).\n\nSo, a\u00b2 +b\u00b2 +c\u00b2=(a +b +c)^2 -54.\n\nThus, to minimize a\u00b2 +b\u00b2 +c\u00b2, we need to minimize (a +b +c)^2.\n\nTherefore, the problem reduces to minimizing (a +b +c)^2 given that ab + bc + ca=27 and abc=23.\n\nThis seems like a problem where we can use inequalities or perhaps consider symmetric functions.\n\nLet me denote S = a + b + c, P = abc =23, and Q = ab + bc + ca=27.\n\nWe need to find the minimum of S\u00b2.\n\nI recall that for positive real numbers a, b, c, the following inequality holds: S\u00b2 \u2265 3Q.\n\nWhich is S\u00b2 \u2265 3*27=81, so S\u00b2\u226581.\n\nThus, the minimal S\u00b2 is 81, achieved when a=b=c.\n\nBut wait, if a=b=c, then 3a\u00b2 +3a\u00b2=54 \u21d2 a\u00b2=6 \u21d2 a=\u221a6\u22482.45.\n\nBut abc= (\u221a6)^3\u22486\u221a6\u224814.7, which is not 23. Thus, equality cannot be achieved.\n\nThus, the minimal S\u00b2 is greater than 81.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps use Lagrange multipliers for the function f(a,b,c)=a +b +c to be minimized under the constraints g(a,b,c)=ab + bc + ca=27 and h(a,b,c)=abc=23.\n\nBut that might be complicated.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps fix two variables and express the third.\n\nLet me suppose that a and b are equal, so let\u2019s set a=b.\n\nThen, 2a\u00b2 + 2ac + c\u00b2=54? Wait, no.\n\nWait, ab + bc + ca=27, with a=b.\n\nSo, a\u00b2 + 2ac=27.\n\nAlso, abc=23 \u21d2a\u00b2c=23.\n\nThus, from a\u00b2 +2ac=27, we can write c=(27 -a\u00b2)/(2a).\n\nSubstitute into a\u00b2c=23: a\u00b2*(27 -a\u00b2)/(2a)=23 \u21d2 (a*(27 -a\u00b2))/2=23 \u21d2 a(27 -a\u00b2)=46 \u21d2 27a -a\u00b3=46 \u21d2 a\u00b3 -27a +46=0.\n\nSolve this cubic equation: a\u00b3 -27a +46=0.\n\nLet\u2019s try possible rational roots: possible roots are factors of 46 over 1, so \u00b11, \u00b12, \u00b123, \u00b146.\n\nTest a=1: 1 -27 +46=20\u22600.\n\na=2: 8 -54 +46=0. Yes! So, a=2 is a root.\n\nThus, factor the cubic: (a -2)(a\u00b2 +2a -23)=0.\n\nThus, a=2, or a\u00b2 +2a -23=0 \u21d2a=(-2 \u00b1\u221a(4 +92))/2=(-2 \u00b1\u221a96)/2=(-2 \u00b14\u221a6)/2=-1 \u00b12\u221a6.\n\nSince a>0, a= -1 +2\u221a6\u22483.45.\n\nSo, a=2 or a= -1 +2\u221a6.\n\nCase 1: a=2.\n\nThen, c=(27 -a\u00b2)/(2a)=(27 -4)/4=23/4=5.75.\n\nThus, a=b=2, c=23/4.\n\nCompute a\u00b2 +b\u00b2 +c\u00b2=4 +4 + (529/16)=8 +33.0625=41.0625=657/16.\n\nCase 2: a= -1 +2\u221a6\u22483.45.\n\nCompute c=(27 -a\u00b2)/(2a).\n\nFirst, a= -1 +2\u221a6.\n\nCompute a\u00b2=(1 -4\u221a6 +24)=25 -4\u221a6.\n\nThus, c=(27 - (25 -4\u221a6))/(2a)=(2 +4\u221a6)/(2a)= (1 +2\u221a6)/a.\n\nBut a= -1 +2\u221a6.\n\nThus, c=(1 +2\u221a6)/(-1 +2\u221a6).\n\nMultiply numerator and denominator by (-1 -2\u221a6):\n\nc=(1 +2\u221a6)(-1 -2\u221a6)/( (-1)^2 - (2\u221a6)^2 )= (-1 -2\u221a6 -2\u221a6 -4*6)/(1 -24)= (-1 -4\u221a6 -24)/(-23)= (-25 -4\u221a6)/(-23)= (25 +4\u221a6)/23.\n\nThus, c=25/23 + (4\u221a6)/23.\n\nCompute a\u00b2 +b\u00b2 +c\u00b2: a\u00b2= ( -1 +2\u221a6 )\u00b2=1 -4\u221a6 +24=25 -4\u221a6.\n\nSimilarly, b\u00b2= same as a\u0