xclusion principle.\n\nTotal number of residents is equal to:\n\n|A \u222a B \u222a C \u222a D| = |A| + |B| + |C| + |D| - |A \u2229 B| - |A \u2229 C| - |A \u2229 D| - |B \u2229 C| - |B \u2229 D| - |C \u2229 D| + |A \u2229 B \u2229 C| + |A \u2229 B \u2229 D| + |A \u2229 C \u2229 D| + |B \u2229 C \u2229 D| - |A \u2229 B \u2229 C \u2229 D|.\n\nBut since D is everyone, any intersection with D is the entire set.\n\nSo, |A \u2229 D| = |A|, |B \u2229 D| = |B|, |C \u2229 D| = |C|.\n\nSimilarly, |A \u2229 B \u2229 D| = |A \u2229 B|, |A \u2229 C \u2229 D| = |A \u2229 C|, |B \u2229 C \u2229 D| = |B \u2229 C|.\n\nAnd |A \u2229 B \u2229 C \u2229 D| = |A \u2229 B \u2229 C| = z.\n\nSo, substituting:\n\n|A \u222a B \u222a C \u222a D| = |A| + |B| + |C| + |D| - (|A \u2229 B| + |A \u2229 C| + |B \u2229 C|) + (|A \u2229 B| + |A \u2229 C| + |B \u2229 C|) - |A \u2229 B \u2229 C|.\n\nSimplify:\n\n= |A| + |B| + |C| + |D| - (|A \u2229 B| + |A \u2229 C| + |B \u2229 C|) + (|A \u2229 B| + |A \u2229 C| + |B \u2229 C|) - |A \u2229 B \u2229 C|.\n\nSimplify further:\n\n= |A| + |B| + |C| + |D| - |A \u2229 B| - |A \u2229 C| - |B \u2229 C| + |A \u2229 B| + |A \u2229 C| + |B \u2229 C| - |A \u2229 B \u2229 C|.\n\nThis simplifies to:\n\n|A| + |B| + |C| + |D| - |A \u2229 B \u2229 C|.\n\nBut since |D| = 900, and |A \u222a B \u222a C \u222a D| = 900.\n\nSo,\n\n900 = |A| + |B| + |C| + |D| - |A \u2229 B \u2229 C|.\n\nTherefore,\n\n900 = 195 + 367 + 562 + 900 - z.\n\nCompute 195 + 367: 562.\n\n562 + 562: 1124.\n\n1124 + 900: 2024.\n\nSo,\n\n900 = 2024 - z.\n\nThus,\n\nz = 2024 - 900 = 1124.\n\nWait, that's 1124, which is more than 900, which is impossible because z is a subset of 900.\n\nThis suggests a miscalculation.\n\nWait, no. Wait, the inclusion-exclusion formula was misapplied.\n\nWait, no, let me think again.\n\nWait, if D is everyone, then |A \u222a B \u222a C \u222a D| = |D| = 900.\n\nBut |A \u222a B \u222a C \u222a D| is equal to |A \u222a B \u222a C|, since D is everyone.\n\nTherefore, |A \u222a B